Package: fastglmm
Title: Fast (Generalized) Linear Mixed Models via the 'glmm' Rust Kernel
Version: 0.5.0
Authors@R:
    person("Paweł", "Lenartowicz", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "pawellenartowicz@europe.com",
           comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0002-6906-7217"))
Description: Fits linear models, generalized linear models, and (generalized)
    linear mixed models with a compiled Rust backend (the 'glmm' crate): linear
    mixed models by REML or maximum likelihood, and Laplace or adaptive Gauss-Hermite quadrature for
    binomial, Poisson, negative-binomial, and Gamma mixed models, using
    'lme4'-style formulas. Estimates are validated against 'lme4', 'glmmTMB',
    and 'MixedModels.jl'. Deliberately scoped to fast fitting - fixed effects,
    Wald standard errors, variance components, and tests of fixed terms and
    of two nested models (anova(), compare()), with an exact restricted
    likelihood-ratio test for one random intercept (Crainiceanu and Ruppert
    (2004) <doi:10.1111/j.1467-9868.2004.00438.x>); anything the backend
    cannot compute honestly (random-effect predictions, profiling) is a
    documented error, never a silently different answer.
